  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single game. Using the given probabilities, let's summarize this in a table.  If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{2}{5})+2(\\frac{3}{10})+3(\\frac{1}{5})+4(\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{4}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{10} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $$2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
